# Kafka transactional control message backfill bug reproduction.
#
# When the last record in a Kafka partition is a transaction control record
# (commit/abort marker), source backfill hangs indefinitely because:
#   - target_offset = high_watermark - 1, which points to the control record
#   - read_committed consumers never deliver control records to the application
#   - The backfill completion condition (offset >= target_offset) is never met
#
# This test requires a Kafka broker (from RISEDEV_KAFKA_BOOTSTRAP_SERVERS)
# and uses a Python script to produce transactional messages.

# This test is run by the Python driver script kafka_txn_backfill.py
# which handles the transactional producer setup (rpk cannot do this).
#
# To reproduce manually:
#   1. Start RisingWave with Kafka: ./risedev d
#   2. Run: python3 e2e_test/source_inline/kafka/kafka_txn_backfill.py \
#             --topic txn-backfill-test --db-name dev --timeout 30
